# --------------------------------------------
# Housekeeping 2026-06-14 (post J-19 v0.14.0 delivery)
# --------------------------------------------

# Per-session ralph-loop driver prompts (canonical convention per discover-execute SKILL.md
# "Write the substituted prompt from Step 3 to .claude/halt-loop-prompts/{slug}.md (gitignored)").
# The canonical halt-loop drivers themselves live under .claude/skills/**/halt-loop-prompts/
# (already exempted via lines 21-22 above for prompts/).
.claude/halt-loop-prompts/

# Vendored reference projects cloned for /discover-execute (large external repos, read-only).
# The line-36 comment mentioned this category but the actual rule (line 170) covered only the
# Portuguese-spelled `referencias/` directory. Adding the English-spelled path closes a 265MB
# leak gap caught during 2026-06-14 housekeeping of flyctl/ + heroku-cli/ + vercel/ clones.
.claude/knowledge-base/references/

# Operator-private loop-state files (extends the `.local.md` convention beyond the 3 specific
# paths at lines 165-167 to cover per-subproject session state like api/.claude/review-loop.local.md
# caught untracked during 2026-06-14 housekeeping). Glob form catches future siblings.
**/*.local.md
api/.claude/

# loop-code-review plugin scratch artifacts. The `final_report.md` per run IS the
# canonical audit trail (cited by ADRs + review reports at known paths) so it stays
# tracked; everything else under code-review-output-*/ is reproducible plugin state:
#   - code-review.db  → SQLite DB, regenerated on each /loop-code-review invocation
#   - analysis/audit/baseline/figures/findings/state/ → per-phase scratch dirs
# Keeping these out of git avoids binary noise + repo bloat across audit cycles.
code-review-output-*/code-review.db
code-review-output-*/analysis/
code-review-output-*/audit/
code-review-output-*/baseline/
code-review-output-*/figures/
code-review-output-*/findings/
code-review-output-*/state/
# Same rule for the bare `code-review-output/` variant (no suffix — plugin default
# when --output-dir is not passed). Kept as separate lines rather than widening the
# glob above so the intent (bare vs suffixed) stays greppable.
code-review-output/code-review.db
code-review-output/analysis/
code-review-output/audit/
code-review-output/baseline/
code-review-output/figures/
code-review-output/findings/
code-review-output/state/

# compiled loopruntime-ops binary (build artifact; source is cmd/loopruntime-ops/)
/loopruntime-ops

# compiled helper binary (regenerable via go build)
tools/gen-service-auth-ed25519/gen-service-auth-ed25519

# loop-cross-validation SQLite working DB (reports are committed; DB is scratch)
cross-validation-output/*.db
.metering-pg.env
halt-loop-prompts/
knowledge-base/implementations/.progress-*.json

# loop-codebase-architect regenerable output (never track — 128KB SQLite + report)
architect-output/
cross-validation-output/

# loop-system-design regenerable output (200KB SQLite, re-derived on each run)
system-design-output/

.review-loop/
.review-runs/

# Build binaries that were versioned by mistake (B-051, 2026-08-11)
tools/loopruntime-dockerfile-lint/loopruntime-dockerfile-lint
operators/app-operator

# Harness session artifacts — neither versioned nor visible to a `git add -A`.
.claude/.compaction-snapshots/
.claude/.patch-backups/

# Kit installer backups — timestamped copies of the previous install, not source.
.claude/.install-backups/

# Kept for history: the kit's installer used to live at `.claude/mechanisms/dist/`
# and the bare `dist/` rules above — meant for build output — swallowed it, so
# this project received the kit without the script that installs or patches it.
# The kit renamed that family to `distribution/`, which no build rule claims, and
# these two lines only matter for checkouts of commits older than that rename.
!.claude/mechanisms/dist/
!.claude/mechanisms/dist/**

# Personal maintenance log, not a project artifact: BACKLOG.md records per-session
# findings for the operator, so it is versioned by nobody and shared with nobody.
# It was tracked until 2026-09-09, when a pull hit a modify/delete conflict between
# a local deletion and remote edits — the ignore rule is what stops that recurring.
BACKLOG.md
.BACKLOG.md.lock

# The Squad kit and the data it writes — a dependency and an output, kept apart.
#
# `.claude/` is an INSTALLED PLUGIN with a repository of its own, so a copy inside a
# consumer is a dependency and not this project's source. Versioning it made every
# adopting repo carry hundreds of permanently dirty files that no `git checkout`
# could settle, because a reinstall rewrites them.
#
# `.squad/` is this PROJECT'S data, which is why it is a separate root: `records/`
# is a dated trail written per machine, and `wiki/` is the consolidated bundle. The
# split exists so the versioning question is answerable for each on its own terms —
# un-versioning the dependency no longer means un-versioning your own knowledge.
#
# `.squad/*` and not `.squad/`: git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so
# the negation below would never fire and new wiki pages would be dropped in silence.
.claude/
.squad/*
!.squad/wiki/
